        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tennis shoes are a perfectly good choice for pickleball, and pickleball shoes are a refinement rather than a different species. Both give you the low, stable platform, lateral support and multidirectional grip the sport needs, which is why either beats a running shoe by a wide margin.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose by surface and fit first: durable outsoles for outdoor hard courts, softer indoor court shoes for gym floors, and a model that holds your heel and midfoot securely. Then pick a pickleball shoe if you want something lighter and play the sport most, or a tennis shoe if you play both or need more size and width options.
          </p>
